          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On May 8, 2009, the GEIPAN received a concise email regarding an observation that occurred during the night of Monday, May 5 to Tuesday, May 6, 2008, between 3 and 4 a.m. No further details will be provided. The direct testimony contains too few details for a proper analysis. Jupiter is present in the southeast (azimuth 128 and 3°48\" elevation) and could be a source of confusion, especially since the witness does not mention it. The perception of motion may be due to the autokinetic illusion: see the link: Perception of movement of a bright point in the sky. This case is classified B: probable misperception with Jupiter.",
